from pathlib import Path
import json
sites={
'rfqdesk':dict(name='RFQ Desk',mark='R',tag='FOR SMALL TEAMS BUYING GOODS',title='Compare the quote.<br><em>See the whole order.</em>',desc='Put supplier prices, minimum orders and freight on the same page. Turn scattered numbers into a clear buying decision.',seo='Free supplier quote comparison & RFQ template | RFQ Desk',side=['Set one product and one currency.','Compare minimum orders, packs and quoted costs.','Export a comparison and a supplier-ready RFQ.'],model='Buyer workspace',price='€19 / month',offer='A proposed workspace for saved quote rounds, supplier history and a reusable approval record. The free comparison and RFQ export work today. The paid workspace is not available.',guide='Compare supplier quotes when MOQs differ',faq=[('Is this a supplier marketplace?','No. Bring your own quotes. We do not verify suppliers, contact them, place orders or arrange payment.'),('Which quote is cheapest?','The table sorts known cash outlay for the calculated order quantity. Extra stock, quality, terms and missing costs can change the actual decision.'),('Does this calculate customs duty?','No. All quotes must use the same currency, equivalent specifications and consistent freight scope. Tax, duty and unquoted charges are excluded.')]),
'modelmeter':dict(name='ModelMeter',mark='M',tag='FOR TEAMS BUILDING WITH AI',title='Know what your<br><em>AI work costs.</em>',desc='Review billed spend by project and model. See where the money goes, check your monthly pace, and take a clean report back to your team.',seo='AI API cost analysis from CSV, without API keys | ModelMeter',side=['Paste normalized usage, with billed USD.','See project costs and a monthly run rate.','Export a review without sharing prompts or keys.'],model='Cost review subscription',price='€29 / month',offer='A proposed subscription for recurring multi-provider imports, project budgets and change alerts. The local CSV review works today. Connections and alerts are not available yet.',guide='AI token estimates versus billed cost',faq=[('Do you connect to my provider?','No. The current tool accepts the documented normalized CSV format. It never requests API keys, sends prompts or changes routing.'),('Are these live model prices?','No. Totals use the billed_usd values you supply. There is no claim that a cheaper model will provide equivalent quality.'),('What does the projection mean?','Spend divided by complete days represented, multiplied by days in the month. It assumes an unchanged pace and excludes any costs missing from your data.')]),
'querysprint':dict(name='QuerySprint',mark='Q',tag='A SMALL PROJECT. A COMPLETE RESULT.',title='From SQL syntax<br><em>to a useful report.</em>',desc='Work through a tiny commerce dataset: filter orders, account for refunds and build a country report. Run real SQL and check your result as you go.',seo='SQL project practice: orders, refunds and revenue | QuerySprint',side=['Explore six fictional order records.','Complete three linked business questions.','Run against two datasets and export your SQL.'],model='Project collection',price='€29 one time',offer='A proposed collection of ten connected SQL projects, data files and worked explanations. This three-step project is free. The project collection is not available for purchase yet.',guide='Build a SQL revenue report that handles refunds',faq=[('Is this a SQL simulator?','Queries execute with SQLite in your browser. Passing means your result matches the expected columns, values and order on two small datasets.'),('Will this get me a job?','This is project practice, not a certification or a promise of employment. Explain your decisions and test further cases before using SQL in production.'),('Can I see a worked solution?','Yes. Hints and solutions are available. Exported work records whether you used them; completion is not presented as an independent assessment.')])}
rfq='''<div class="fields"><div><label for="quantity">Required units</label><input id="quantity" type="number" min="1" value="300"></div><div><label for="currency">One quote currency</label><select id="currency"><option>USD</option><option>EUR</option><option>GBP</option></select></div></div><label for="product">Product name</label><input id="product" maxlength="160" placeholder="e.g. 750 ml insulated bottle"><label for="destination">Delivery location</label><input id="destination" maxlength="200" placeholder="City, country, postal code"><label for="specs">Specifications for the RFQ</label><textarea class="short" id="specs" maxlength="3000" placeholder="Material, size, finish, quality requirements…"></textarea><label for="quotes">Supplier quotes CSV</label><textarea id="quotes" maxlength="1000000" spellcheck="false" placeholder="supplier,unit_price,moq,pack_size,freight,setup,lead_days"></textarea><p class="quiet">All prices in the selected currency. Blank costs are unknown and will be rejected; enter 0 only if confirmed. Use one product with equal specifications.</p><div class="actions"><button id="compare">Compare my quotes</button><button class="secondary" id="template">CSV template</button><button class="secondary" id="rfq">Download RFQ</button></div>'''
model='''<div class="fields"><div><label for="budget">Monthly budget · USD</label><input id="budget" type="number" min="0.01" value="300"></div><div><label for="days">Complete days represented</label><input id="days" type="number" min="1" max="31" value="14"></div><div><label for="month">Days in this month</label><select id="month"><option>28</option><option>29</option><option selected>30</option><option>31</option></select></div><div><label for="customers">Active customers</label><input id="customers" type="number" min="1" value="40"></div></div><label for="file">Open normalized usage CSV</label><input id="file" type="file" accept=".csv,text/csv"><label for="usage">Or paste usage CSV</label><textarea id="usage" maxlength="1000000" spellcheck="false" placeholder="project,provider,model,requests,input_tokens,output_tokens,billed_usd"></textarea><p class="quiet">One row per request or disjoint aggregate. Do not mix overlapping totals or currencies. Remove keys, prompt text and personal data. Up to 10,000 rows / 1 MB.</p><div class="actions"><button id="analyze">Analyze my costs</button></div>'''
sql='''<div id="steps" class="steps"></div><h3 id="title"></h3><p id="brief"></p><details><summary>Dataset and schema</summary><pre>orders(id INTEGER, customer TEXT, country TEXT, status TEXT, revenue REAL, refund REAL)</pre><p class="quiet">Fictional records. Both revenue and refund use the same arbitrary currency. A second dataset checks that the query is not tied to these numbers.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="data"></table></div></details><label for="sql">Your SQL query</label><textarea id="sql" spellcheck="false" maxlength="6000"></textarea><div class="actions"><button id="run">Run &amp; check SQL</button><button class="secondary" id="hint">Show hint</button><button class="secondary" id="solution">Show worked solution</button></div>'''

def wrap(slug,title,desc,body,path='/'):
 d=sites[slug];return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{title}</title><meta name="description" content="{desc}"><link rel="canonical" href="https://{slug}.agiscorecard.com{path}"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css"><meta name="theme-color" content="#20332f"></head><body data-site="{slug}"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header><a class="brand" href="/"><span>{d['mark']}</span>{d['name']}</a><nav><a href="/#workbench">Workbench</a><a href="/guide">Guide</a></nav></header>{body}<footer><span>{d['name']} · Free tool / early product experiment</span><a href="/privacy">Privacy &amp; product status</a><a href="/guide">How it works</a></footer></body></html>'''
for slug,d in sites.items():
 side=''.join(f'<li>{s}</li>' for s in d['side']);faq=''.join(f'<article><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></article>' for q,a in d['faq'])
 sample='<button id="sample" class="secondary">Try fictional sample</button>' if slug!='querysprint' else '<span class="pill">SQLite · no signup</span>'
 extra='<div class="stats"><div><strong id="spent">—</strong><span>billed USD in this file</span></div><div><strong id="projected">—</strong><span>monthly pace · USD</span></div><div><strong id="percustomer">—</strong><span>pace / customer · USD</span></div></div>' if slug=='modelmeter' else '<p class="eyebrow" id="progress">0 / 3 completed</p>' if slug=='querysprint' else ''
 body=f'''<main id="main"><section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">{d['tag']}</p><h1>{d['title']}</h1><p class="lead">{d['desc']}</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#workbench">Open the free workbench ↗</a></div><p class="quiet">No signup. Your working data stays in this browser.</p></div><aside class="mini"><span class="pill">FREE / BETA</span><ol>{side}</ol><a href="/guide">{d['guide']} →</a></aside></section><section id="workbench" class="workbench"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">WORKBENCH</p><h2>A result you can use.</h2></div>{sample}</div><div class="editor"><div class="inputs">{dict(rfqdesk=rfq,modelmeter=model,querysprint=sql)[slug]}</div><div class="output">{extra}<div id="status" role="status" class="status">Start with your data or explore the clearly marked fictional example.</div><div class="table-wrap"><table id="results" aria-label="Results"></table></div><div class="actions"><button id="export" disabled>Download my result</button></div><p class="quiet">Review the assumptions before using your result.</p><label class="consent"><input type="checkbox" id="measurement">Share anonymous usage steps to help improve this tool. Working data is never included. Optional; off by default.</label></div></div></section><section id="offer" class="offer" hidden><p class="eyebrow">PROPOSED PAID PRODUCT · NOT OPEN</p><h2>{d['model']}</h2><p class="price">{d['price']}</p><p>{d['offer']}</p><button id="interest">This would be useful at this price</button><p class="quiet">This button sends anonymous price interest only. No purchase, email signup or reservation.</p><p id="interest-status" role="status"></p></section><section class="below">{faq}</section></main><script type="module" src="/app.mjs"></script>'''
 p=Path('site')/slug;p.mkdir(exist_ok=True);(p/'index.html').write_text(wrap(slug,d['seo'],d['desc'],body))
 privacy=f'''<main id="main" class="article"><p class="eyebrow">PRODUCT STATUS · 18 SEPTEMBER 2026</p><h1>Useful tools.<br>Clear boundaries.</h1><h2>Your working data</h2><p>{d['name']} runs its free workbench in your browser. Quotes, cost rows, SQL queries and TradeCheck document data are not uploaded. TradeCheck MCP downloads run locally, but your AI assistant may send supplied documents to its own model provider. The server receives the requests needed to serve the site. Cloudflare, the hosting provider, may process network and security information.</p><h2>Optional measurement</h2><p>Usage measurement is off by default. If you enable it, we send an event name, site, source category, sample/exercise/own-data label and a random identifier for this page visit. We store no entered content, email, API key or IP address in the experiment database. Events are deduplicated within the visit and kept in a 35-day active window. Older records are deleted on the next measurement request; if there are no requests, they can remain longer. There is no cross-site profile. Closing the page discards the browser's visit identifier. Disabling the checkbox stops future optional events.</p><p>The optional past-30-day question submits only the chosen answer category (none, once, or twice or more), with the same anonymous visit fields. The price-interest button explicitly submits an anonymous interest event even when general measurement is off. A success message appears only if the server records it. It does not subscribe you, charge you or reserve a product. Anonymous counts cannot establish distinct buyers or revenue.</p><h2>What is available</h2><p>The free workbench is available. The proposed paid product is not for sale. We have not claimed customers, savings, job outcomes or verified suppliers. The displayed proposed price is a research hypothesis, not a checkout quote.</p><h2>About this experiment</h2><p>This tool is part of the AGI Scorecard project. Use the <a href="https://agiscorecard.com/">main project site</a> for project information. You can use every free function without sharing optional events. Downloaded files stay on your device.</p><a class="button" href="/">Return to the workbench</a></main>'''
 (p/'privacy.html').write_text(wrap(slug,'Privacy and product status | '+d['name'],'How this free experiment handles working data and optional measurement.',privacy,'/privacy'))
 (p/'robots.txt').write_text(f'User-agent: *\nAllow: /\nDisallow: /api/\nSitemap: https://{slug}.agiscorecard.com/sitemap.xml\n')
 (p/'sitemap.xml').write_text('<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">'+''.join(f'<url><loc>https://{slug}.agiscorecard.com{x}</loc></url>' for x in (['/','/guide','/privacy','/agent','/agent-guide'] if slug=='rfqdesk' else ['/','/guide','/privacy']))+'</urlset>')
Path('experiments.json').write_text(json.dumps({k:{'name':v['name'],'host':k+'.agiscorecard.com','proposed_price':v['price'],'model':v['model'],'sales_enabled':False} for k,v in sites.items()},indent=2)+'\n')
guides={
'rfqdesk':'''<h2>Start with the same buying question</h2><p>A unit price is not a complete quote. Compare one product, equivalent specifications, one currency and freight to the same location. If a supplier has not quoted a fee, ask first; a blank is not zero.</p><h2>The calculation</h2><pre>order units = ceil(max(required units, MOQ) / pack size) × pack size\nknown cost = order units × unit price + freight + setup\nunit cost = known cost / order units</pre><p>For 300 required units, a quote at $2.10 with MOQ 500 and pack size 100 requires 500 units. With $250 freight and $50 setup, known cash outlay is $1,350. Another quote at $2.45 with MOQ 200, pack size 50, $90 freight and no setup requires 300 units and $825. The lower unit price needs more cash and leaves 200 extra units.</p><h2>Ask for the missing terms</h2><p>Record quote validity, production and shipping time separately, quality requirements, payment schedule and the named place for the agreed shipping terms. The RFQ export prompts these questions; it does not send them or create a supplier agreement.</p><h2>What this comparison excludes</h2><p>Tax, duty, insurance, inspection and other unquoted costs are excluded. Currency conversion is not provided. This is arithmetic from your inputs, not a customs estimate or supplier recommendation. Do not compare quotes with incompatible freight scope.</p><h2>Beyond the spreadsheet</h2><p>The useful next step is a repeatable quote round and approval history. A marketplace would additionally require real suppliers, verified buyer demand and an agreed transaction process. None of those is implied by this calculator.</p>''',
'modelmeter':'''<h2>Start from what was billed</h2><p>Headline input/output token rates may not capture caching, reasoning, tools or the provider actually used. <a href="https://openrouter.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/51691717731483-Why-was-I-charged-more-per-token-than-the-price-shown-on-the-model-page">OpenRouter's billing explanation</a> describes these dimensions. Use recorded billed amounts when reviewing actual spend.</p><h2>Prepare the CSV</h2><pre>project,provider,model,requests,input_tokens,output_tokens,billed_usd\nSupport,Example provider,Fast model,1000,200000,50000,4.50</pre><p>This is our normalized format, not a promise to accept every provider export unchanged. Use either request rows or disjoint aggregates. Combining both counts the same spend twice. Convert amounts to USD outside the tool using a documented method before import; do not relabel another currency as USD.</p><h2>Interpret the monthly pace</h2><p>If the file contains $140 for 14 complete days in a 30-day month, the linear pace is $300. This does not predict growth, incident retries or future model mix. A per-customer average is a rough allocation: uneven customer usage needs a customer-level breakdown.</p><h2>Where this tool fits</h2><p>This is an offline review of a file. It does not enforce budgets or monitor live traffic. <a href="https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/proxy/cost_tracking">LiteLLM spend tracking</a>, <a href="https://langfuse.com/pricing">Langfuse</a> and <a href="https://www.helicone.ai/pricing">Helicone</a> already offer broader tracking options. Use their official pages to evaluate current limits and pricing.</p><h2>Before changing models</h2><p>Lower spend is useful only if the task still succeeds. Compare cost per accepted task, retries and latency on your own evaluation set before changing production routing. This tool does not measure model quality.</p>''',
'querysprint':'''<h2>Turn a business question into a sequence</h2><p>The project asks a narrow question: how much net revenue did paid orders produce, and in which countries? Start by deciding what an eligible row is, then define the measure, then choose the grouping.</p><h2>1. Select the relevant rows</h2><p>Cancelled orders are excluded. A fully refunded paid order still belongs to the paid set, with net revenue of zero. The status filter and refund calculation serve different purposes.</p><h2>2. Define the measure</h2><pre>net revenue for a row = revenue - refund</pre><p>Summing revenue alone ignores refunds. Subtracting refunds both before and after aggregation counts them twice. The exercise uses non-null values in one currency; a real dataset also needs explicit decisions about tax, currencies, chargebacks and missing data.</p><h2>3. Group and order</h2><p>Group paid rows by country and sum their net amount. Name the calculated column net_revenue. Sort by that value descending; use country ascending for ties to make the result deterministic.</p><h2>Check another dataset</h2><p>A query that returns one correct total by coincidence is weak evidence. Each exercise runs against two fictional datasets. That catches some hardcoded answers and refund mistakes, but does not prove correctness on all possible data. Download the SQL and add cases of your own.</p><h2>Keep learning</h2><p>For more syntax practice, try <a href="https://sqlbolt.com/">SQLBolt</a>. For the exact SQLite behavior used here, read the <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/lang_select.html">SQLite SELECT documentation</a>. Our original exercise is a small project, not a complete course or certification.</p>'''}
for slug,body in guides.items():
 d=sites[slug];html=f'<main id="main" class="article"><p class="eyebrow">PRACTICAL GUIDE</p><h1>{d["guide"]}</h1>{body}<a class="button" href="/#workbench">Try the free workbench</a></main>'
 (Path('site')/slug/'guide.html').write_text(wrap(slug,d['guide']+' | '+d['name'],d['guide'],html,'/guide'))
